---
// The keys that open the command menu, beside the button that opens it (Header.astro). Barlow has
// no ⌘, so the command key is drawn, an SVG of the key's symbol, and only the letter is text (ADR
// 0025). The drawing is hidden from assistive technology and the letters are not: in the bar the
// keys are all a sighted visitor sees of the button, so its name holds them, "Command menu Ctrl
// K", as a name must hold the visible label (SC 2.5.3), and a voice saying "Ctrl K" finds it.
// Until 2026-10-30 the keys were hidden too, and the name was "Command menu" alone.
// aria-keyshortcuts on the button tells the keys as well. src/scripts/palette.js names the keys of
// the keyboard at hand once it binds the button, which stays unseen until then: "Ctrl K" on a PC,
// the drawn key and "K" on an Apple keyboard.
---

<kbd class="keys" data-keys>
  <svg class="key-command" viewBox="0 0 12 12" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
    <path d="M4 4V2.6A1.6 1.6 0 1 0 2.6 4H4zm0 0h4M4 4v4m0 0H2.6A1.6 1.6 0 1 0 4 9.4V8zm0 0h4m0 0v1.4A1.6 1.6 0 1 0 9.4 8H8zm0 0V4m0 0h1.4A1.6 1.6 0 1 0 8 2.6V4z" />
  </svg>
  <span data-keys-text>Ctrl K</span>
</kbd>
